# UFF-DA EATS - Command Center / Square setup
#
# This root file is a SETUP REFERENCE, not a deployment mechanism. The Vite app
# runs in command-center/ and DOES NOT load this root .env.example or .env.local.
# Copy command-center/.env.example to command-center/.env.local for local Vite
# development. The deployed GitHub Pages app reads the public runtime values
# in command-center/public/live-orders-config.js.
#
# Public browser values (configured in command-center/.env.local for local use):
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://xgyqjnfdqekwlofhtpcj.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_YOUR_PUBLIC_KEY
#
# IMPORTANT: live-orders-config.js takes precedence over local VITE_* values.
# To test a different Supabase project locally, edit that public runtime config
# in your local checkout. Never put a secret or Square token in VITE_* or in
# live-orders-config.js: both are visible to every visitor in browser assets.
#
# Server-only values: enter these in Supabase project Order Manager under
# Project Settings -> Edge Functions -> Secrets. Do not put their values in
# GitHub Pages, command-center/.env.local, this file, or any tracked file.
#
# SQUARE_ACCESS_TOKEN=<Production access token for your Square seller account>
# SQUARE_LOCATION_ID=<Production location ID used on your truck iPhones>
# SQUARE_WEBHOOK_SIGNATURE_KEY=<Production webhook subscription signature key>
# SQUARE_WEBHOOK_NOTIFICATION_URL=https://xgyqjnfdqekwlofhtpcj.supabase.co/functions/v1/square-webhook
# ALLOWED_ORIGIN=https://elliotttmiller.github.io
#
# In the Square Developer Console PRODUCTION environment subscribe to:
# payment.created, payment.updated, order.created, order.updated.
# Use exactly the SQUARE_WEBHOOK_NOTIFICATION_URL above as the subscription URL.
# The signature calculation includes the exact URL, including trailing slash.
# A Sandbox token cannot fetch real iPhone payments: this integration calls
# Square's production API at https://connect.squareup.com.
#
# Hosted Edge Functions receive SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY and
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY from Supabase automatically. Do not configure a
# database URI, pooler or service-role key in the browser. A PUBLIC Supabase
# publishable key is safe in the browser; it is not a secret key.
#
# Test: sign in at /foodtruck/command-center/#/live-orders, choose Refresh from
# Square, and verify one real paid iPhone order including name and modifiers.
# Until that succeeds, the green Live board indicator only confirms that the
# browser reached the database; it does not prove Square is connected.
